 isitors through Bayview’s cultural landmarks\, creative businesses\, and
  artist spaces. The celebration starts with a Historical Tour & Art Walk l
 ed by April Spears-Mays\, Executive Director of the Cultural District.\nGu
 ests will explore key cultural sites along Third Street and connect with l
 ocal artists and Black‑owned businesses\, with featured stops including 
 Let’s Eat BBQ\, the San Francisco SFAAACD Hub\, and the Bayview Makers S
 hop on Third Street. These stops highlight the intersection of art\, food\
 , culture\, and entrepreneurship that continues to shape Bayview. The tour
  begins at the Bayview Opera House at 3:00 PM and concludes at the SFAAACD
  Hub at 5:00 PM.\n\nFollowing the art walk\, guests will gather for a comm
 unity reception and dinner at Tato’s Kitchen SF from 5:00–7:00 PM\, on
 e of the neighborhood’s beloved Mexican restaurants. The reception featu
 res food\, conversation\, and live music\, bringing together artists\, res
 idents\, cultural workers\, and community supporters. Performers include D
 J Leydis\, Batuki\, and Yrak Sáenz\, with Gina Madrid serving as host.\nT
 he evening culminates at the historic Ruth Williams Opera House with the 5
 th Annual Afro‑LatinX Concert\, produced by La Fauna Music and hosted by
  Oakland artist and cultural organizer Gina Madrid. More than a concert\, 
 it’s a cel...\n\n$20.00\n\nTickets: https://rwoh.org/upcoming-events/\nD
