CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSan Francisco International Ar
 ts Festival (SFIAF) is pleased to announce the start of the fifth season o
 f The Last Supper Party\, curated by Alameda Poet Laureate Kimi Sugioka. T
 he season opens on Saturday\, October 3\, at 6 p.m. at Muddy Waters Coffee
  & Lounge (521 Valencia Street\, San Francisco\, CA 94110). The evening fe
 atures poetry by Sara Biel and Tureeda Ture Ade Mikell\, accompanied by mu
 sic from singer-songwriter\, Tony Aldarondo and friends.\nAt The Last Supp
 er Party\, SFIAF invites audiences to share ideas and bread and find inspi
 ration in the thoughts and words of artists and writers whose perspectives
  are drawn from a kaleidoscope of cultures\, but who are united by compass
 ion and a common desire to seek justice\, equity\, and truth.\n\nThe Octob
 er 3 program is presented as part of Fall of Freedom (a nationwide arts mo
 vement that calls on artists\, institutions\, and communities to resist au
 thoritarianism through exhibitions\, performances\, and public events) and
  the Mission Arts Performance Project (MAPP — a free community-run arts 
 and music night that has spent more than 20 years celebrating the Mission 
 District’s culture).\nThe Last Supper Party series takes place on the fi
 rst Saturday of the month in collaboration with the San Francisco Planning
  Department and its Mission Action Plan 2030. The series will be presented
  at a different venue along the 16th Street Corridor every month from Octo
 ber through May. The goal of the collaboration with the...\n\nFree\n\nTick
 ets: https://www.sfiaf.org/lsp_oct_3_2026\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.co
 m/supper-party-free-poetry-music-bread-mission/\nSource: Funcheap SF
