DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T152500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17830215@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:No band embodies the soul and spirit of Hardly Strictly Bluegr
 ass more directly—or more literally—than Marco and The Polos. On Sunda
 y\, October 4 at Hardly Strictly Bluegrass 2026\, the beloved Bay Area ens
 emble will join forces with Hills to Hollers\, an East Bay supergroup feat
 uring Barbara Higbie\, Vicki Randle\, and Laurie Lewis\, for a special col
 laboration celebrating the rich and diverse roots of Americana music.\n\nE
 volving over the lifespan of the festival and fronted by the children of f
 ounder Warren Hellman\, what began as a front-porch jam has grown into a f
 ully formed musical collective characterized by intricate four-part harmon
 ies that blend and resonate the way only family singing can.\n\nHellman si
 blings Frances\, Marco\, Patricia\, and Judith perform heartfelt originals
  interspersed with unexpected folk and rock covers\, accompanied by a vete
 ran band featuring fingerstyle guitarist Stevie Coyle\, multi-instrumental
 ist Barbara Higbie\, bassist and musical director Joshua Zucker\, and voca
 l director Amber Morris. As comfortable gracing festival stages as they ar
 e in intimate listening rooms\, the group has established itself as a main
 stay of the Bay Area acoustic music scene and a beloved fixture at Hardly 
 Strictly Bluegrass.\n\nHills to Hollers explores the rich intersection of 
 cultural and musical influences across the spectrum of the American folk t
 radition. Soulful\, explosive\, unpredictable\, and fun\, the group has be
 en featured at the Kate Wolf Music Festival\, Wintergrass\, and...\n\nFree
 \n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/marco-and-the-polos-wit
 h-hills-to-hollers-at-hardly-strictly-bluegrass-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
