DESCRIPTION:SF Game Development is excited to be hosting an event during S
 F Tech Week with a hands-on session from Discord on building community aro
 und your game. Don't miss this unique opportunity to learn from an industr
 y expert\, who will take the stage at 7:00 pm.\n\nBuilding Your Discord Se
 rver Through Every Stage of Game Development Anthony Tešija\n\nThe best g
 ame communities start long before launch day. Learn how to build a communi
 ty and evolve it through your game's alpha\, release\, and beyond. We'll c
 over channels\, roles\, events\, moderation\, and how to bring players str
 aight from your game into your community and keep them engaged.\n\nAnthony
  will walk through the four stages every game passes through -- in develop
 ment\, alpha/beta\, release\, and post-release -- and what your server sho
 uld actually look like at each one: why starting minimal beats over-buildi
 ng\, how forum channels turn scattered feedback into organized bug reports
 \, how community invites can auto-assign your beta testers\, and how Rich 
 Presence and bots can bridge your game and your server to turn players int
 o organic marketing.\n\nFree\nSF Game Development presents\n\nTickets: htt
 ps://www.dnalounge.com/calendar/2026/10-06a.html\nDetails: https://dotheba
 y.com/events/2026/10/6/sf-tech-week-building-your-discord-server-tickets\n
