DESCRIPTION:It’s not very well-worn\, but the Nashville street band to c
 omposer pipeline has certainly been a distinctive\, if tempered\, fairy-ta
 le arc for Joshua Kaufman and Justin Rubenstein\, the brothers at the helm
  of The Blasting Company. For years\, curiosity and circumstance guided th
 em through the streets of the US and Europe as they accumulated a blend of
  American folk and Eastern European influences\, grand orchestral tendenci
 es\, and inescapably modern sensibilities\, eventually landing them in Los
  Angeles\, where they found a home for most of it in the world of film and
  television. Their first and perhaps most notable venture into scoring was
  for the critically-acclaimed animated miniseries\, Over the Garden Wall\,
  which has become a seasonal staple for a growing fanbase worldwide whenev
 er fall - or its equatorial approximate - is in the air. Other composing v
 entures include music written for Burlesque\, the New York Times/ Serial p
 odcast The Kids of Rutherford County\, Adult Swim’s The Elephant\, and a
  threealbum soundtrack for table top role playing campaign\, The Crooked M
 oon. Their recent releases feature collaborations with Tom Kenny (Spongebo
 b Squarepants)\, Haley Reinhart (Post-Modern Jukebox)\, Jemaine Clement (F
 light of the Concords)\, and one of their all-time musical heroes\, arrang
 er and composer Van Dyke Parks. The Blasting Company's journey has been on
 e dedicated to their artistic community and their craft. This\, and the ea
 gerness with which they explore music’s expansive storyt...\n\nGoldenvoi
 ce Presents\n\nTickets: https://tix.axs.com/BTg4EgAAAAD39SXFAgAAAAAJ%2fv%2
 f%2f%2fwD%2f%2f%2f%2f%2fC0dvbGRlbnZvaWNlAP%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f?c
 id=usaffdostuff\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-blast
 ing-company-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32918907/49ebeae5-5f9d-4038-9b2b-353b7dd2841f.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-blasting-company-tickets
END:VEVENT
