BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Julia Jacklin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17432200@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nNorth America Tour 2026
 \nJulia Jacklin\n\nFriday\, October 23 | The Castro\n\nJulia Jacklin is ce
 lebrated for her emotionally direct lyricism\, captivating performances\, 
 and commanding voice. Since the release of her acclaimed debut Don’t Let
  The Kids Win (2016)\, Jacklin has become one of the most respected artist
 s in contemporary independent music\, with follow-up albums Crushing (2019
 ) and PRE PLEASURE (2022) — the latter debuting at #2 on the ARIA Charts
 . Across her career\, she has earned two ARIA Awards and had thirteen nomi
 nations and widespread international critical acclaim\, with both Crushing
  and PRE PLEASURE landing on numerous year-end best-of lists and receiving
  universal praise from outlets including Pitchfork\, Rolling Stone\, NME\,
  MOJO\, and Uncut.\n\nA formidable live performer\, Jacklin has built a su
 bstantial global touring audience through sold out headline shows at venue
 s including London’s Roundhouse\, Melbourne’s Forum\, and Brooklyn Ste
 el in New York\, alongside appearances at major festivals such as Glastonb
 ury\, Primavera Sound\, Austin City Limits\, Pitchfork Music Festival\, an
 d Laneway. In addition to extensive headline touring\, she has shared stag
