BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When Manilatown Swung: The Manila Serenaders
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17914041@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:WHEN MANILATOWN SWUNG: THE MANILA SERENADERS\n\nWhat did Manil
 atown sound like when Kearny Street was alive with music?\n\nStep into the
  sounds and stories of historic Manilatown for a special Club Mandalay: Mu
 sic\, Memory & Manilatown gathering featuring live jazz\, archival photogr
 aphs\, family memories\, and community Talk Story at the International Hot
 el Manilatown Center.\n\nAt the heart of the afternoon is Canuto Salaver\,
  a drummer with the Manila Serenaders whose life was deeply connected to h
 istoric Manilatown and the I-Hotel. Members of the Salaver Family join gue
 st interviewer Sabrina Oliveros to share family stories passed down about 
 Canuto-his life around Kearny Street\, his connection to the Bataan Cafe a
 nd Poolhall\, and his years making music with the Manila Serenaders.\n\nTh
 e musical lineage continues with Raymond Bambao\, bassist with today's Man
 ilatown Jazz Ensemble\, whose grandfather and grand-uncles also played wit
 h the Manila Serenaders.\n\nThroughout the afternoon\, the Manilatown Jazz
  Ensemble brings these histories back into sound with live musical interlu
 des inspired by the era\, while photographs and materials from the Manilat
 own Archives and family collections bring the world of historic Manilatown
  into view.\n\nAudience members will also be invited into the Talk Story-b
 ecause the memories carried by our families and communities are part of ho
 w history lives.\n\nAnd because history can be fun: Feeling festive? Come 
 dressed in your 1930s-40s finest! Period-inspired attire...\n\nFree\nManil
 atown Heritage Foundation\n\nTickets: https://www.manilatown.org/all-event
 s/when-manilatown-swung-the-manila-serenaders\nDetails: https://dothebay.c
 om/events/2026/10/24/when-manilatown-swung-the-manila-serenaders-tickets\n
 Source: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7961254;-122.4049416
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34760555/2e9d19c1-f4ef-4641-8d0a-3d3facc90124.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:I-Hotel Manilatown Center in SF\, 868 Kearny St\, San Francisco\,
  CA\, 94108
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/24/when-manilatown-swung-the-manil
 a-serenaders-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s “Golden Hour” Filipino Night Market is Back for 2026 (S
 oMa)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639069@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Undiscovered SF\n\n​✦ UNDISCOVERED SF\nSan Francisco’s F
 irst Night Market Is Back\n​Ten years ago\, Undiscovered started the tre
 nd of night markets. Now\, we return during golden hour.\nRSVP – FREE\n
 ​This year marks a special milestone — join us as we celebrate 10 seas
 ons of community\, creativity\, and cultural pride! For our second hub\, w
 e are so excited to bring back UNDISCOVERED SF Season 10: the Golden Hour 
 Night Market in partnership with Victory Hall.\n\n​Nestled in the fabled
  Ritch Street Alley\, Victory Hall has been a cornerstone of SoMa since 19
 08 — home to the legendary 330 Ritch Nightclub and a long legacy of musi
 c\, community\, and culture in partnership with Deanna Sison\, a culinary 
 trailblazer\, a custodian of Filipino tradition\, and an influential force
  in San Francisco’s hospitality scene.\n​On October 24\, we’re honor
 ed to be part of that legacy — filling Ritch Street with Filipino Americ
 an food\, art\, music\, and culture in the heart of the Filipino Cultural 
 Corridor.\n#UNDSCVRDseason10 #MadewithMahal\n​✦ Come hungry. Come read
 y to move. Come discover.\n​\n​Eat your way through the market\, shop 
 retail vendors\, catch DJ sets\, and step inside Victory Hall for a specia
 l exhibition honoring the history of 330 Ritch\, the legendary nightclub t
 hat once made this block pulse after dark.\n​✦ Anchored by Mestiza and
  Victory Hall\, UNDSCVRD Golden Hour Night Market is an intimate but elect
 ric return: a celebration of ten years of Undiscovered\, the flavors of ou
 r community\, and the people who...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://luma.com/r
 aipa01b\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-golden-hour-filipino-night-m
 arket-2026-soma/\nSource: Funcheap SF
