DESCRIPTION:SF’s Civic Music Free Concerts (2026)\nSF Civic Music Associ
 ation\nThe San Francisco Civic Music Association is dedicated to offering 
 numerous opportunities for classical music lovers and amateur musicians in
  the San Francisco Bay Area.\nOur ensembles are open to all musicians and 
 our concerts are free and available to the public. We’d love to see you 
 soon!\n\n2026 SCHEDULE & PROGRAM\nSunday\, October 18\, 2026 – SF Civic 
 Symphony: Great Mysteries\nHerbst Theatre\, 401 Van Ness Ave\, SF – maps
 \n3:00 PM – 5:00 PM\nPROGRAM:\n\nFranz Liszt: Les Préludes\nCamille Sai
 nt Saëns: Cello Concerto No. 1\, A minor\nAngela Lee\, Cello\nEdward Elga
 r: Enigma Variations\n\nPaul Schrage – Music Director & Conductor: Paul 
 Schrage\nRSVP | Free Concert – Donations Accepted – Suggested Donation
  $20\nSunday\, October 24\, 2026 – An Afternoon of Chamber Music\nNoe Va
 lley Ministry\, 1021 Sanchez St\,. SF – maps\n3:00 PM – 5:00 PM\nPROGR
 AM:\n\nMarcel Boucard\, Suite Champêtre\nBarbara Landt\, Flute\nCarol Yar
 brough\, Horn\nPaul Hindemith\, Kleine Kammermusik\nMalcolm Arnold\, Three
  Shanties\nSonore Quintet\n– Barbara Brown\, Flute\n– Susan Ritter\, O
 boe\n– Sam Torrisi\, Clarinet\n– Jeff Dickey\, Horn\n– Leigh Korn\, 
 Bassoon\nAntonín Dvořák (1841–1904)\, Piano Quartet No. 2 in E♭Majo
 r\nPinky Quartet:\n– Leyan Lo\, Violin\n– Alex Li\, Viola\n– Eric Ch
 eng\, Cello\n– Sheila Chan\, Piano\n\nRSVP | Free Concert – Donations 
 Accepted – Suggested Donation $20\nSunday\, November 1\, 2026 – Civic 
 Strings: Enlightenment and America\nFirst Baptist Church\, 22 Waller St.\,
  SF – maps\n3...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://buytickets.at/sanfranciscoc
 ivicmusicassociation/2401078/r/fun-cheap\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com
 /sfs-civic-music-free-concerts-2026-3/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/DSC017
 93.webp
