DESCRIPTION:Día de los Muertos\nSaturday\, November 7 | Davies Symphony H
 all\n\nJoin us for a celebration of Latin American music and culture inclu
 ding lobby installations by local artists. The dynamic concert program\, c
 onducted by José Luis Gómez\, features traditional music with contempora
 ry works honoring the rich heritage of this ancient holiday. The event is 
 curated by longtime collaborator Martha Rodríguez-Salazar\, and features 
 longtime artistic partner Casa Círculo Cultural.\n\nLights Along the Path
 : Day of the Dead in Tlaxcala\nThe San Francisco Symphony\, in collaborati
 on with curator Martha Rodríguez-Salazar and artistic partner Casa Círcu
 lo Cultural\, is proud to present the 2026 Día de los Muertos exhibit\, L
 uces en el Camino: Día de los Muertos en Tlaxcala\, at Davies Symphony Ha
 ll on Saturday\, November 7\, 2026.\n\nInspired by the cultural traditions
  of Tlaxcala and the symbolism of the firefly\, this year’s exhibition e
 xplores themes of remembrance\, resilience\, renewal\, and hope\, and will
  feature altar installations and visual artworks that honor loved ones\, c
 elebrate ancestral connections\, and illuminate the paths that guide us th
 rough times of uncertainty.\n\nThis celebration goes far beyond one day: E
 ach year\, we invite local artists to craft installations and altars honor
 ing both the living and the deceased. Curated by Martha Rodríguez-Salazar
 \, these installations aim to commemorate the Day of the Dead by connectin
 g us across centuries and continents and exploring what Mexican and Latin.
 ..\n\nTickets: https://sfsymphony.org/Buy-Tickets/2026-27/Dia-de-los-Muert
 os\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/dia-de-los-muertos-tick
 ets\nSource: DoTheBay
