BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kino
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17222536@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Born in the underground clubs of Leningrad in 1981\, KINO beca
 me the defining voice of Soviet rock — a band that smuggled freedom into
  every chord when freedom itself was contraband. Fronted by the magnetic V
 iktor Tsoi\, they played to 62\,000 at Moscow's Luzhniki Stadium in 1990. 
 Months later\, Tsoi was gone. The music never stopped. "What Elvis Presley
  was to America\, Tsoi was to Russia." Now\, original members Yuri Kaspary
 an\, Alexander Titov\, and Igor Tikhomirov bring KINO back to the stage 
 — accompanied by Tsoi's own voice\, restored and digitized from original
  multi-track recordings. This is not a tribute act. This is KINO\, continu
 ing the conversation. Expect anthems you know by heart — Gruppa Krovi\, 
 Peremen\, Posledniy Geroy — performed with the raw urgency that made the
 m timeless. Sung in Russian. Felt in every language.\n\nAll Ages\nEventCar
 tel Presents\n\nTickets: https://www.axs.com/events/1394481/kino-tickets?s
 kin=warfield&src=AEGLIVE_WWRFLSFO022715VEN001?cid=usaffdostuff\nDetails: h
 ttps://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/kino-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7827039;-122.4103578
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/31489798/c2f5e8a1-a5d4-45d8-b343-60843eccdf9a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Warfield\, 982 Market St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/kino-tickets
END:VEVENT
